WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.320
Between Netflix, Amazon, cable networks, and
every other way to watch T.V. these days,

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.200
there's a real wealth of great stories out
there for fantasy fans — many of which have

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.340
been on the air for some time.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.629
So whether you're looking for fairies, witches,
or ancient gods, here are the best fantasy

00:00:14.629 --> 00:00:16.660
shows that you still might not be watching.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.560
Amazon has made a few splashy entries into
the fantasy genre over the last few years,

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.140
but Carnival Row might be their most ambitious
project yet.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.760
Based on a film script by showrunner Travis
Beacham, the show tells the story of a mythical

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.120
world where a group of supernatural creatures
called "fae" are forced to integrate into

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.640
human society after war strikes their community.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.899
Naturally, this creates plenty of discord
between the two populations, especially considering

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:45.300
that humans are immediately distrustful of
this group of powerful, magical beings.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.540
Of course, it also doesn't help that there's
a supernatural serial killer running around,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.040
either.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.900
The show is packed with plenty of star power,
including Orlando Bloom, Cara Delevingne,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.700
and Jared Harris.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.280
So if you're looking for a series that beautifully
blends magic with mystery and murder, then

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.920
you might just want to take a stroll down
Carnival Row.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.420
Time travel is always a great conceit for
any fantasy show, since it allows characters

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:12.420
to freely travel across all kinds of different
worlds and eras, and Starz' hit series Outlander

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.660
uses this device to perfect effect.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.640
Based on Diana Gabaldon's book series, this
adaptation stars Caitriona Balfe as Claire

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:24.180
Randall, a married nurse who's just survived
World War II, only to find herself transported

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.340
back to Scotland in 1743 by a set of magical
stones.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.780
Trapped in a time where women have no rights
or any autonomy, Claire tries to find her

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.980
way back home — but soon falls for Jamie
Fraser, a Highlander she marries for protection.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.300
As their bond deepens, Claire begins to resist
the chance to return home, eventually trying

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.080
to manipulate time itself to keep the two
lovers together.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.820
Thanks to its steamy central romance, captivating
characters, and exciting story, the show has

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:53.390
been a huge success for Starz, serving as
one of the cable network's biggest hits and

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.760
earning rave reviews from critics since it
premiered in 2014.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.140
So if you're looking for romance, adventure,
and attractive people with British accents,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.760
then don't worry — Claire and Jamie have
got you covered.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.599
As one of the most popular American novelists
of today, Neil Gaiman's work is always ripe

00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:14.670
for adaptation, and in 2019, Amazon became
the official home of Good Omens, a show based

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:18.730
on Gaiman's groundbreaking collaboration with
the legendary Terry Pratchett.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:23.629
It's the story of an angel named Aziraphale
and a demon called Crowley, who must work

00:02:23.629 --> 00:02:28.020
together to stop the impending apocalypse
— as they've gotten pretty comfortable inhabiting

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.330
their human bodies on Earth.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.090
Ultimately, this show has everything fantasy
fans could possibly want, bringing its religious

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.750
elements and ethereal action into play in
a quirky, whimsical way that thrives on the

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.280
chemistry between David Tennant and Michael
Sheen.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.460
Good Omens was an immediate hit when it premiered
on Amazon Prime in May 2019, with critics

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.000
praising its humor in particular.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.500
With just six episodes, now is as good a time
as ever to binge this quick, funny series

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.140
that balances light humor with the heaviest
of stakes.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.280
“To the world."

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.100
"To the world."

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.519
As Good Omens has shown, Neil Gaiman adaptations
have proven to be pretty fertile television

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.680
ground over the past couple of years — but
perhaps the biggest and boldest of any Gaiman

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.880
TV show is American Gods, based on his 2001
novel of the same name.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.520
The show follows the saga of Shadow Moon,
an ex-convict who's drawn into a conflict

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.060
between the new and old gods.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:27.099
And as he encounters leprechauns, hammer-wielding
deities, and the personification of the media,

00:03:27.099 --> 00:03:31.580
he's shepherded along by Mr. Wednesday, a
charming yet mysterious con man who sits right

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.290
in the heart of this pan-religious war.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:37.180
"When you strike lightning you should expect
consequences."

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.489
With a knockout cast and a rock solid story,
it's no wonder that American Gods has been

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:43.700
a hit since its 2017 premiere.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.860
Ever since Riverdale burst onto the scene
in 2017, becoming one of the most talked about

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.819
shows on television, it's been clear that,
somehow, Archie comics still offer a deep

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.140
well of material to pull from.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:58.900
Once Riverdale proved it was a bona fide sensation,
showrunner Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa teamed up

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.220
with Netflix to develop The Chilling Adventures
of Sabrina, based on another Archie comic.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.580
Starring Mad Men's very own Kiernan Shipka,
the show takes on a much darker tone than

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.800
you might remember from the lighter Melissa
Joan Hart Sabrina series.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.020
As a half-witch, this new Sabrina Spellman
is constantly struggling to find a bridge

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.140
between her two worlds.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.979
Putting Sabrina's fantastical identity crisis
at the forefront and mixing that with romance,

00:04:20.979 --> 00:04:26.310
intrigue, action, and horror has proven incredibly
successful for this fledgling show, and thanks

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:30.260
in large part to Shipka's grounding performance,
the series has received glowing reviews.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:35.760
The first adaptation of Deborah Harkness'
wildly popular All Souls trilogy of novels,

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.979
UK series A Discovery of Witches premiered
with an eight episode season in September

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.340
2018, delighting Harkness fans and newbies
alike.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.560
Initially set at Oxford University, the series
chronicles the journeys and adventures of

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:50.780
Diana Bishop: a historian trying to deny her
true identity as a witch, who comes across

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.280
a haunted tome in the university's library
and finds herself swept into a world of magic

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:55.980
and monsters.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.160
With the help of a vampire-scientist named
Matthew Clairmont, Diana must embrace her

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.030
heritage and fight her prejudice against vampires
as they team up to not only protect the book,

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.850
but explore its mysteries to the fullest.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:10.291
Though Warner Brothers initially acquired
the rights to A Discovery of Witches for a

00:05:10.291 --> 00:05:15.139
film adaptation, the UK network Sky One eventually
bought the rights, turning it into a series

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:15.640
of their own.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.919
And that seems to have been a pretty smart
move on their part, as the show currently

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:21.919
has a 100 percent approval rating on Rotten
Tomatoes.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.460
If you're not in the UK, you can check out
the show on both AMC and BBC America.

